### Storage-Provision (Python Flask app on each storage node)

#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///c:/Users/Punith/LaaS/host-services/storage-provision/app.py)

**Safety guard**: Add an NVMe-oF target check to `list_files()` and `get_storage_usage()` before the on-demand mount logic. If the zvol's NVMe-oF subsystem exists in configfs (`/sys/kernel/config/nvmet/subsystems/laas-<uid>`), the zvol is being served to another node — **refuse** to mount it locally.

```python
# Before on-demand mount in list_files() and get_storage_usage():
subsystem_path = f"/sys/kernel/config/nvmet/subsystems/laas-{storage_uid}"
if os.path.exists(subsystem_path):
    return jsonify(error="Storage is currently accessed via cross-node NVMe-oF. "
                         "File operations should be routed to the compute node."), 409
```

This is a **safety net** — normally the backend will route away from storage-provision during cross-node sessions. But if something bypasses routing, this prevents corruption.

